// An ExecutionEnvironment mixing a NESTED entry with a SINGLE one crashes the parser with a
// NullPointerException, in either order. Each form ALONE parses.
//
//   E1  nested only            -> OK
//   E2  single only            -> OK
//   E3  nested, then single    -> NullPointerException
//   E4  single, then nested    -> NullPointerException
//
// The grammar admits both under one `executions` list -- `executions: (singleExecEnv |
// multiExecEnv)*` -- so this is a combination it accepts and the walker cannot handle. An
// NPE is not a diagnostic: it names no element, no line and no construct, so a model author
// hitting it is told only that something was null.
//
// Uncomment E3 or E4 to reproduce; E1 and E2 are the controls.
###Service
ExecutionEnvironment demo::E1
{
   executions:
   [
      PROD:
      [
         primary: { mapping: demo::M; runtime: demo::RT; }
      ]
   ];
}

ExecutionEnvironment demo::E2
{
   executions:
   [
      UAT: { mapping: demo::M; runtime: demo::RT; }
   ];
}

// ExecutionEnvironment demo::E3
// {
//    executions:
//    [
//       PROD: [ primary: { mapping: demo::M; runtime: demo::RT; } ],
//       UAT: { mapping: demo::M; runtime: demo::RT; }
//    ];
// }
